  "findings": [
    "Whole IrishHolidays source reconstructs exactly from its before copy through the two existing February branches plus the explanatory comment. February 1 receives the existing bank label on Monday or Friday only from 2023; first Monday excludes day 4 and pre-2023 years. All other holiday, Easter, Calendar input and label bytes remain unchanged.",
    "The first Monday is February 4 exactly when February 1 is Friday. The fixed February 1 branch handles that Friday exception and Monday February 1 without the earlier saint-only return suppressing the bank label. Other February 1 observances retain the saint label.",
    "The live 12-method test is byte-identical to the frozen test. Seventeen literal Gregorian dates also assert supplied Calendar immutability. Original baseline XML has 12 testcase children, four intended org.junit.ComparisonFailure outcomes and eight controls; candidate leaf has 12 actual cases and no negative outcomes.",
    "Baseline admission corrects an initial wrapper classifier that required the exact AssertionError type: ComparisonFailure is an AssertionError subtype. The same original failed terminal/XML was admitted, with no baseline rerun or assertion change.",
    "CalendarPacks.headerLines directly calls IrishHolidays.forToday(now) when the existing Irish pack is enabled, then prefixes the nonempty label. Current consumer inspected and bound; no settings or display change is required.",
    "Build terminal reports exit 0 without timeout in 103.167858542s; build log includes JVM/debug/performance/R8/vital success. Independent full XML replay finds 4585 actual testcase children in 477 suites, matching headers, zero failure/error/skipped outcomes.",
    "Whole build.gradle reconstructs from before bytes by only 170→171 and 1.176→1.177. Both candidate APK lengths and SHA256 independently match the retained artifact receipt. The bound root verifier records package com.immortal.launcher.debug and unchanged signer 4f9a3b1d0c86028e831add351642a6167d06e9d3ed6ded6dcf5a790a560b45d6 for both exact APKs.",
    "Independently decoded ZIP payloads for both candidates and retained 1.176 baselines. All 23 source assets match current source, receipt and baseline bytes; asset entry sets agree. Debug assets are exact; performance changes only assets/dexopt/baseline.prof with preserved pro-NUL header."
  ],
